 1.Introduction
 ===============

 Version 1.0

 Headerselect - a little helpfull-Tool for CNet/3.
 It selects randomly ansis from a little pool of your ansis.
 Not tested with CNet`s older than V3.05c!! But it should work.
 
 Headerselect is CallMeWare! If you use it, please give us a call!
 VISION THING BBS  - +49-(0)-345-663914
 CONFUSION BBS     - +49-(0)-341-6896640.

 2.Contents of this Archive
 ==========================

 You need:

 headerselect.rexx    -   main program
 headerselect.doc     -   this document
 ansis/               -   directory including some ansis for Headerselect 

 3.Installation
 ==============

 Installation of Headerselect is very easy!
 Make a Directory in your Pfiles called KeksDesign 
 Copy the files in this directory.

 Well, lets come to the most important facts.
 Headerselect needs the information which type of ansi it should use!
 There are f.i. Upload, Download, Start, End, FileArea, Mailarea...
 First of all you need at least one ansi of the type you wanna use!
 (ofcoz :-)) put this ansi in a directory (see configuration for the
 directory!) and name it: menu.1 (if thats a menu ansi!)
 the next menu ansi is called menu.2, then menu.3 .... got it?
 then you can make upload.1, upload.2, ..., download.x, start.x .....

 If you use it for the Menu,  put this in line 67 (CNET/3.05c).
 line must be look like this:       

 #0pfiles:keksdesign/HeaderSelect.rexx Menu}*0systext:sys.mainmenue}
 ^-----> ctrl + q of course!             ^---kind of ansi!
                                                                      
 if you use it for upload, download etc.,            
 and put this line in the SysText:sys.upload (download, end...)       

 #0pfiles:keks/headerselect.rexx upload}                             
 with the argument (here upload) you chose the kind of ansi.
 Easy, isnt it?
 If you use it in the file area, just edit the entry text of the area and
 write the following line in the entry text: (surprise :-))
 #0pfiles:keks/headerselect.rexx filearea}                             

 Well, it`s very easy. But remember you need at least one ansi of the kind
 you wanna use!

 4.Configuration
 ===============

 As mentioned before the ansis have to be in a directory. You can make this
 directory in the pfiles:keksdesign/ directory or (like I did) in the
 envarc: directory, for not too much `busyness` of the HD :-)

 In the headerselect.rexx there is a line where you can change the
 directory of the ansis.

 Thats it!

